From 0abd4aee7fbb42d949b3e64337327227892cf307 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:34:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Arp Ball: the plates part faster, the last hits further apart
 (kBallPartFactor 1.5 -> 1.9)

After the buzz each parting gap now about triples (1 - r_p = 1.9 (1 - r); with bounce +7 r_p = 0.335): at 138 BPM
over two beats 16, 32, 97, 289 ms instead of 22, 24, 52, 108, 228 ms. Measured in Pettra "You Are The Seeds" with a
net of gammatone resonators on the arp's notes (references/pettra-arp/net.py): after its fastest hits the figure
slows down by about three times per hit, 10, 20, 60, 150-210 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/deluge/modulation/arpeggiator.h | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/modulation/arpeggiator.h b/src/deluge/modulation/arpeggiator.h
index 202bdca7..c15ed158 100644
--- a/src/deluge/modulation/arpeggiator.h
+++ b/src/deluge/modulation/arpeggiator.h
@@ -54,8 +54,9 @@ constexpr float kRollMinGapSamples = 706.0f;
 // measured under its bass (references/pettra-arp/METHODS.md); 15 ms is the buzz that came closest by ear
 constexpr float kBallMinGapSamples = 661.0f;
 // A ball's plates part faster than they close in: each parting gap grows by 1 / r_p with 1 - r_p = this times 1 - r,
-// so the ball ends slower than it started, as the figure in Pettra does
-constexpr float kBallPartFactor = 1.5f;
+// so the ball ends slower than it started. 1.9: after the buzz the gaps about triple per hit, as the figure in Pettra
+// does (10, 20, 60, 150-210 ms, measured with references/pettra-arp/net.py)
+constexpr float kBallPartFactor = 1.9f;
 constexpr uint32_t kMaxRollHits = 255;
 
 // How a bouncing ratchet's velocity follows its gaps (the numbers are what songs store, 0 and 1 as the old on/off)
